2026-10-09T02:14:05.9639363Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9647929Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9724020Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9731857Z [0m
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9732246Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9732607Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9732729Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9733116Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9733627Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9733874Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9734092Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9734543Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9734694Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9735071Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9735538Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9735910Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9736200Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9736339Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9736536Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9736742Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9736969Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9737183Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9737256Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9737329Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9737418Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9737629Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9738079Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9742956Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9743081Z I will:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9743180Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9743355Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9743718Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9744098Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9744596Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9744828Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9745071Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9745541Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9745856Z    /root
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9756985Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9757422Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9766545Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9767100Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9767340Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9768686Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9769026Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9783240Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9783829Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9792195Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9792705Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9792987Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9793096Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9793204Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9793328Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9793475Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9793818Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9793993Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9794089Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9794448Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9794697Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9794961Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T02:14:05.9795368Z   $ sh ./install-nix
